---
description: Keep backend TypeScript and Express code layered by responsibility.
globs: apps/**/src/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

# Backend TypeScript

- Keep the flow: routes → controllers → services → repositories → database.
- Routes define endpoints; controllers translate HTTP; services hold domain logic; repositories access persistence.
- Do not put SQL, Prisma queries, or domain calculations in controllers.
- Keep framework code at the edge; do not leak Express request/response objects into service methods.
- Validate external input at the HTTP boundary before it reaches business logic.
- Use explicit TypeScript types and keep modules focused on one responsibility.
